CSS BACKGROUND-POSITION
======================
Background-position decides WHERE the background image sits inside an element.

Pause & think:
Does this change image size? → No
Does this stop repeating? → No


DEFAULT BEHAVIOR
================q
If you write nothing, the image starts from the top-left.

Think:
Top-left of image touches top-left of element.

background-position: 0% 0%;


KEYWORD POSITIONS
=================
Keywords act like magnets.

left    → stick to left edge
right   → stick to right edge
top     → stick to top edge
bottom  → stick to bottom edge
center  → stick to center


Try in your head:

background-position: center;

Question:
Where is the image now?
→ Center of the element


Two-keyword examples:

background-position: top right;
background-position: bottom left;


HOW KEYWORDS WORK
=================
Rule to remember:

First value  → horizontal
Second value → vertical

Single keyword case:

background-position: right;

Think:
Right edge horizontally,
center vertically.


PIXEL VALUES
============
Pixels = pushing the image.

background-position: 20px 40px;

Stop & imagine:
- Push image 20px from left
- Push image 40px from top


PERCENTAGE VALUES
=================
Percentages align points, not edges.

background-position: 50% 50%;

Think:
Image center meets
element center.


NEGATIVE VALUES
===============
Negative values pull the image outside the box.

background-position: -20px -10px;

Result:
- Image moves left
- Image moves up


BACKGROUND-POSITION WITH COVER / CONTAIN
========================================
Size decides HOW BIG, position decides WHICH PART.

background-size: cover;
background-position: center;

Question:
Which part stays visible?
→ Center of the image


MULTIPLE BACKGROUND IMAGES
=========================
Each image can be positioned independently.

.layered {
    background-position: center, top left;
}

Think:
First image → center
Second image → top-left


IMPORTANT RULE (LOCK THIS)
==========================

background-position → placement
background-size     → scaling
background-repeat   → tiling

They NEVER replace each other.


BEST PRACTICE
=============
Never rely on default positioning.

Safe habit:

.box {
    background-position: center;
}


COMMON MISTAKES
===============
Ask yourself:
- Did I forget default is top-left?
- Am I expecting resize?
- Did I mix up value order?
- Did I forget position with cover?


PRACTICE (DO THIS)
==================
Use one image.
Change only background-position.
Do not touch size or repeat.

Observe:
The image moves,
but never resizes.

.box {
    height: 250px;
    background-image: url("images/photo.jpg");
    background-position: center;
}
